a Virgin Atlantic plane was forced to  make an emergency landing in Boston last  night after a fire broke out in the  cabin flight 138 left New York's JFK  Airport around eight o'clock headed for  London's Heathrow Airport it was  diverted though to Boston's Logan  Airport after smokes smoke and flames  were coming from a passenger's seat  police say a battery pack for a cell  phone charger between the seats may be  to blame crew members put out the fire  and all 217 passengers on board were  evacuated safely in Boston no serious  injuries
 

